\tag{foundation}
\tag{augmented}

\p{This follows \ref{augmented-comparison} under \ref{dec-kr-0015}, \ref{dec-kr-0018}, \ref{dec-tl-0021} and \ref{at-fd-0007}. It fixes the vertical category and horizontal graph; \ref{augmented-generating} now extends it to a global free mapping property. The arity nerve remains open.}
\subtree{
  \title{Checked construction}
  \p{\code{CellOperation.Position} is finite and boundary-indexed. \code{CellInterpretation.interpret_operations} recovers the original incident operations. \code{Operations.Map} preserves identities and substitution, with ordinary equality after explicit transport. Its equation-preservation results include arbitrary nested rows.}
  \p{\code{CellTerm.Related} is the congruence generated by exactly the five augmented equation families. \code{evaluate_related} proves soundness in every lawful algebra. \code{quotient_laws} proves the laws on the quotient itself by lifting complete rows and nested rows through a section. \code{freeAlgebra} is consequently lawful without assumed quotient laws. \code{freeLiftEquiv} proves the universal mapping property for cell generators over this fixed incidence.}
  \p{\code{CellTerm.Leaf} is finite for each raw term; \code{evaluate_eq_of_leaves} shows evaluation depends only on these generator occurrences. Finiteness alone is not an arity theorem.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Remaining arity obligations}
  \p{The fixed base is not the generating presheaf category required by the global augmented construction: \ref{augmented-generating} supplies that base, freely generated vertical paths and the global mapping property. The category of arities, its density and nerve recognition, any generic/free factorization used, and its elementary core presentation remain unproved. The required labelled diagram model has not started. No gate statement is weakened, no canonical encoding is declared, and \ref{at-fd-0007} remains proposed at statement-version 1.}
}
\p{Reproduce with \code{lake build Augmented} and \code{python3 scripts/check_foundations.py}; see \code{docs/augmented/README.md}. The declaration inventory audits the full import closure against the approved axioms. Cites: \ref{dec-kr-0014}, \ref{dec-rt-0030}, \ref{dec-wf-0008}, \ref{dec-wf-0010}.}
